{:adr-id "2607155000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-4311 (demolition of buildings and other structures) demolition-project-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607150700" "ADR-2607011000" "ADR-2607142800" "ADR-2607152000"]

 :context
 "cloud-itonami-isic-4311 did not exist prior to this ADR (verified via gh repo view
  before starting -- no failed prior attempt to recover from). ISIC Rev.5 class 4311
  is Demolition -- a safety-critical domain (structural-collapse risk, hazardous
  materials such as asbestos/lead), confirmed against the authoritative
  kotoba-lang/industry registry (id 4311 = 'Demolition') before scaffolding, avoiding
  the code-mislabel failure mode ADR-2607154000 (isic-0145) hit. cloud-itonami-isic-
  4211 (Community Building Construction) was read in full as the primary structural
  template -- it establishes this fleet's robotics premise and module shape (facts/
  governor/notify/operation/phase/registry/sim/store + advisor, plus 4211-specific
  robotics/simphysics modules simulating a physical robot mission). This task
  explicitly required a NARROWER design: demolition is construction/heavy-equipment-
  adjacent, so per this workspace's standing rule against new Rust/robot-control code,
  cloud-itonami-isic-4311 was scoped coordination-only from the start -- no robotics/
  simphysics analog, no module committing a real-world actuation effect. Every
  proposal carries :effect :propose unconditionally; the governor HARD-holds anything
  else -- a structural invariant distinguishing this actor from every prior
  cloud-itonami-isic-* actor (including 4211), whose actuation ops DO commit real
  effects. Built by reading cloud-itonami-isic-4211 in full, adapting its module shape
  to demolition, with clojure -M:test independently re-run before and after every
  push, matching the stricter verification protocol of the preceding ISIC-coverage
  batch."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["heavy-equipment control (dispatching or commanding equipment) -- outside this
   actor's authority entirely; the closed op-allowlist cannot express it, and the
   governor's forbidden-action-class HARD check independently rejects any proposal
   carrying an :equipment-control?/:direct-actuation? marker, un-overridable by any
   human approval"
  "structural-engineering-decision / demolition-plan-finalization authority -- the
   licensed engineer / site supervisor's exclusively; :schedule-demolition-operation
   proposes a phase-window schedule, never a finalized engineering plan; the same
   forbidden-action-class check rejects a :finalizes-engineering-plan? marker"
  "real-world actuation of any kind -- every committed record carries :effect
   :propose only (effect-not-propose HARD check, defense-in-depth against a
   compromised/malfunctioning advisor)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-4311 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Notify,
  Advisor, Phase, Operation, Sim (structured after cloud-itonami-isic-4211
  module-for-module where applicable, narrowed to coordination-only authority):
  - Governor (Demolition Governor): 8 hard checks (unknown-op, effect-not-propose,
    forbidden-action-class, site-not-verified, legal-basis-missing,
    hazmat-survey-incomplete, notification-lead-time-insufficient [quantitative
    jurisdictions only], unresolved-safety-concern) + high-stakes escalation
    (:flag-safety-concern and :schedule-demolition-operation ALWAYS escalate
    unconditionally at every phase; :order-supplies escalates above a $5000 USD cost
    threshold or below the 0.6 confidence floor)
  - Facts: per-jurisdiction (JPN/USA/DEU) hazmat-survey/demolition-notification
    legal-basis catalog, citing REAL official sources verified via web search before
    writing: Japan's 石綿障害予防規則第3条 + 建設リサイクル法第10条 (7-calendar-day
    notice), USA's OSHA 29 CFR 1926.1101 + 40 CFR 61.145 NESHAP (10-working-day
    notice), EU/Germany's Directive 2009/148/EC Art.11 (honestly :qualitative, no
    fabricated numeric lead-time) transposed via GefStoffV/TRGS 519.
    notification-lead-insufficient? is the same three-valued ground-truth recheck
    family construction.facts/weather-threshold-exceeded? established
  - Registry: pure-function site-record-log/schedule-proposal/safety-concern-flag/
    supply-order-proposal drafts (jurisdiction-scoped sequence numbering) +
    render-safety-concern-notice (human-readable document, legal basis inline,
    explicitly disclaims plan-finalization authority)
  - Store: Store protocol, dual MemStore/DatomicStore (langchain.db), contract-tested
    for parity. DatomicStore uses langchain-store.core (ADR-2607141600) for the
    EDN-blob codec/identity-schema/event-log pattern via a data-driven entity
    field-spec instead of hand-rolling enc/dec* -- a NEW store, so it follows the
    current convention rather than the hand-rolled pattern earlier actors predate.
    Unlike every sibling actor, no history is double-actuation-guarded -- every op
    may recur any number of times per site, since this actor never actually
    dispatches/authorizes/files/hands over anything
  - Notify: mail+phone (Resend+Twilio) Notifier protocol, structurally identical to
    construction.notify but fires only after human approval of :flag-safety-concern
    (never on an auto-commit path)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + deterministic mock-advisor (default) + llm-advisor
    (real-inference seam), all four ops carry :effect :propose
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate; :log-site-record/:order-supplies are the ONLY ops ever
    in a phase's :auto set (phase 3); :schedule-demolition-operation/:flag-safety-
    concern permanently absent from every phase's :auto set
  - Operation: langgraph-clj StateGraph actor, real interrupt-before human-in-the-loop
    + checkpoint resume, structurally identical to construction.operation
  - Sim: demo driver (clojure -M:dev:run), 8 seeded sites, full episode + all 8
    HARD-hold paths + cross-jurisdiction (USA) + qualitative (DEU/EU) walkthrough
  - Operations: log-site-record (survey/hazmat-assessment/progress data logging,
    auto-eligible), schedule-demolition-operation (ALWAYS escalates),
    flag-safety-concern (ALWAYS escalates), order-supplies (cost-threshold-gated)
  - Tests: 68 tests / 252 assertions, all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop in src), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY domain-adapted for
    demolition coordination -- NOT copy-pasted from 4211's own SECURITY.md/
    CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, which were found to carry leftover HR/talent-domain language
    from a shared template"

 :consequences
 {:positive
